;; The plan. HYPOTHETICAL. Nothing here was spent.
;;
;; One file per project under ledger/planned/, included below, matching ledger/spent/.
;; A plan and the hours that answer it belong to the same project, so they are filed the
;; same way: a task lands in the book of the repository it will be done in, and the two
;; can be read side by side without either being a subset of one big file.
;;
;; The unit is PLANNED-SECONDS, not SECONDS, and that is the split doing real work
;; rather than a label asking to be believed. Beancount will not balance across
;; commodities, so a planned second cannot be netted against a spent one, summed
;; with one, or quietly become one: the tool refuses it at parse time. The account
;; separation and check_docs.py's gate sit on top of that as belt and braces.
;;
;; Every amount below is an estimate of work nobody has done, so it is booked as a
;; liability -- an obligation outstanding -- and never as an expense. Expenses are
;; seconds that went somewhere, and they live in ledger/spent/, which git
;; generates. The two files share no account by construction, and check_docs.py
;; fails if they ever do, because a planned second that reads as a spent one is a
;; plan reporting itself as progress.
;;
;; Do not add the two together. `Liabilities:Planned:Mesh` is what is owed and
;; `Expenses:Delivery:Mesh` is what was paid; a sum of them is neither.
;;
;; Only two things are planned: the first task and the last. Everything between
;; them is guesswork about a state nobody has observed yet, and writing it down
;; makes it look decided -- which is how OPEN_GAPS.md carried 231/234 for eight
;; weeks after the code reached 1360/1360, and how two planning documents
;; inherited that number without re-deriving it. The next first task is chosen
;; when this one closes and the state is known.
;;
;; Accomplished tasks stay, marked `done`, so the file records what closed rather
;; than only what is left. `ledger.py path` skips them.
;;
;; Estimates are three-point, te = (o + 4m + p) / 6, with o and p at the 1st and
;; 99th percentile -- the range the Daniels fit memo argues for and the F-35 uses.
;;
;; The percentiles are Bayesian, not empirical. Session length is modelled as
;; lognormal with a Jeffreys prior, so o/m/p are quantiles of the posterior
;; predictive for the next session of that size. That matters at the tail: the
;; empirical 1st and 99th percentiles of the 5-9 bucket are its smallest and
;; largest observations, one session each, and reading a plan off a single
;; observation is how a p99 comes out narrower than the truth. The posterior
;; predictive carries uncertainty about the parameters as well as the spread, and
;; is wider wherever the evidence is thin -- 91,872 s against an empirical 50,724 s.
;;
;; One modelling choice dominates the answer and so is stated rather than buried.
;; A session's cost is the span from its first commit to its last, which excludes
;; everything before the first commit, so spans near zero are censored rather than
;; short. They are floored at fifteen minutes: two commits took at least that. The
;; p99 for a 2-4 commit task reads 38.91 h at a one-minute floor, 10.91 h at
;; fifteen, and 7.49 h at thirty. Fifteen is a judgement, the sensitivity is the
;; evidence, and a censored likelihood would replace both.
;;
;; Actual hours never land here -- they land in delivery.beancount, from git -- so
;; the plan cannot quietly become a claim about what happened.

option "title" "fabric-plan: HYPOTHETICAL, the critical path to a mesh a player can trust"
option "operating_currency" "PLANNED-SECONDS"

;; The lane the budget is set against. The per-project books open leaves beneath it, and
;; beancount rolls them up, so the budget bounds the mesh rather than any one repository.
2026-08-16 open Liabilities:Planned:Mesh  PLANNED-SECONDS
2026-08-16 open Equity:Plan               PLANNED-SECONDS

;; The last task. Not estimated: it is the condition that closes the thread, and a
;; number against it would be a guess about work that has not been scoped.
2026-08-16 event "deliverable" "A player draws a closed curve in VR, gets a mesh back, and the mesh is correct by a check that can fail"

;; The budget: one working week, 40 hours, fixed. The scope is not.
;;
;; Sizing a scope in advance is the average-pilot error. A cockpit built for the
;; mean pilot fit none of the 4,063 Daniels measured, and the fix was not a better
;; mean, it was adjustment. This plan has the same shape: the same five tasks cost
;; 13.81 h at the median and 51.24 h at the 99th, a spread of nearly four to one,
;; so a scope chosen for either number is wrong for the other. Fix the budget and
;; let the scope slide.
;;
;; The rail, taken in order. Cumulative total effort at 99%:
;;
;;   1. P0  link geogram on macOS            10.98 h
;;   2. E   run the pipeline once            16.07 h
;;   3. A   the differential gate            31.14 h
;;   4. B   boundary triangulation           ~41    h
;;   5. G   clusterIncidence determinism     51.24 h
;;
;; Work down it and stop where the week runs out. At the median all five fit inside
;; 40 h with room; at the 99th only the first three do. Which is true is not known
;; in advance, which is the whole reason the scope adjusts instead of the budget.
;;
;; Only the notch being worked is written as a task below. The rest are the rail,
;; not commitments, because an estimate written down as a plan reads as a decision
;; -- which is how OPEN_GAPS carried 231/234 for eight weeks.
;;
;; The survey says this is the right week to buy. Six of fifteen responses name
;; creation in one slot or the other -- a meshing pen, user generated content,
;; moddable, absolute interactability, and save-and-share twice -- the largest
;; cluster in it, and the one this deliverable serves. The same memo applies there:
;; those six did not name a feature, they named the adjustment mechanism, which is
;; what lets holly have fishing and dragos have his horde without either choosing.
2026-08-16 custom "budget" Liabilities:Planned:Mesh "weekly" 144000 PLANNED-SECONDS

2026-08-16 note Liabilities:Planned:Mesh "Scope slides, budget does not. Stop at whichever notch of P0-E-A-B-G the 40 h runs out on; all five fit at the median and only the first three at the 99th, and which holds is not known until P0 reports."

include "planned/Patch-Verify.beancount"
include "planned/Fabric.beancount"
